WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.639
The written word can be a powerful tool.

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:09.450
It has been used to speak truth to power,
to allow readers to journey to distant stars,

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:14.710
and to explore the forbidden love triangle
between a human girl, a vampire, and a werewolf,

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.740
in my personal favorite book series of all
time.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:23.670
Literature can be a truly incredible force,
and like anything capable of enacting great

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.500
change, it can be used for good or for evil.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.300
In August of 2006, the home of the leader
of a religious group known as the “Church

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.329
of True History” was raided by authorities.

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:41.400
There, they found a variety of illegal materials,
but they also discovered a collection of books.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:47.930
One of the books found was a 450-page hardcover
book entitled, “Chronicle of the 20th Century.”

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:52.510
Though it looked like an ordinary history
book, concerns surrounding the religious group

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.940
and its leader led the police to analyze its
contents more carefully.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:01.350
And if you’re familiar with a certain other
anomalous chronicle, you may start feeling

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.370
nervous right about now.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:10.000
The book’s publisher was listed as Interworld
Press, located in Chicago, IL, but an investigation

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.850
into the publishing company revealed that
the company was never registered in the United

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:15.850
States.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:21.390
Not only that, but the street it was supposed
to be located on didn’t even exist.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:26.189
One officer, a man named Detective Carl Jones,
was assigned to read through the book and

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:30.149
take thorough notes on anything else unusual
he might find.

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:35.450
The book consisted largely of newspaper clippings
and short articles, covering significant events

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:40.090
from January of 1900 to December of 1995.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:44.920
As Jones flipped through the book, he found
that it was well-written, thoroughly researched,

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.870
and most importantly, it was largely accurate
to recorded history.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:54.119
At least, it was, until he reached 1956.

00:01:54.119 --> 00:02:00.500
From around June 15, 1956, onward, the events
described began to veer off course.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:05.100
They did not match any version of history
Jones was familiar with or anything he had

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.560
even heard about.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.160
It went from a standard retelling of history,
to a sincere account of what appeared to be

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.330
an alternative version of history.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.990
The strangeness did not end there.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:22.700
Jones’s colleagues noticed that as his examination
of the book progressed, he began to behave

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.750
erratically.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.980
He expressed confusion, and his demeanor took
on a dazed quality.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:32.920
He would make statements about events from
the book as if they were fact, and when corrected

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:37.720
by one of the other officers, would become
frustrated and overwhelmed.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.220
He began to have violent outbursts, throwing
a coffee cup against the wall while arguing

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.920
with another man assigned to the case with
him.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:50.300
He overturned his desk chair, knocked papers
to the floor, and even tore out pieces of

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.590
his own hair.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.570
He was given a psychological evaluation, and
found to be struggling with panic attacks,

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.340
nightmares, and paranoia.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.770
Still, Jones insisted that he continue to
read through the book.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:07.060
As he continued to read, fellow officers noticed
that it was not only his mental state that

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.300
was affected.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.300
His physical state began to change as well.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.670
Dark circles formed under his eyes, a clear
sign of exhaustion, a scar appeared on his

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.780
cheek where there had previously been only
smooth skin.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:26.220
His knuckles became bloodied, though he swore
up and down that he had done nothing to cause

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.220
it.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.880
While sitting at his desk, the officers stationed
nearest to Jones heard something small clatter

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.040
to the floor.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:39.250
He looked up, and found that several of Jones’s
teeth had fallen out, for seemingly no reason.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:45.130
Finally, and most horrifically, Jones collapsed
to the floor and became unresponsive.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.650
He was rushed to the hospital, where he died
within hours.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:54.280
An autopsy produced more questions than answers
as his cause of death was declared: radiation

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.300
poisoning.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.340
The police officers on the case proceeded
to interrogate the religious leader they had

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:04.540
apprehended, looking for clues into the mysterious
demise of their fallen colleague.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.850
He said only that he had owned the book for
two years, and that he imbibed illegal substances

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.090
to “hide from the truth.”

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:16.730
A week later, he slipped into a coma, presumably
from withdrawal, and died shortly after.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.600
The police were at a loss for explanations.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.520
How could a book cause this much damage?

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:27.140
Only one officer among the group had any inkling
of what to do here - And that was because

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:31.930
they were actually an undercover field agent
embedded in the precinct by the SCP Foundation.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:37.770
The book was soon whisked away, the relevant
figures were given amnestic treatment to forget

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.690
what they had seen, and the dangerous tome
was logged onto the Foundation database under

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:46.130
a new name - SCP-592.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:52.320
SCP-592 appears to be a perfectly ordinary
book at first glance, but it has been shown

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.010
to cause delusions, paranoia, and a variety
of physical changes from small shifts in appearance

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:01.370
to extreme, even deadly, wounds.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:05.140
Understanding that the book possessed anomalous
properties, the Foundation set to work trying

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:09.540
to determine how exactly those properties
worked, and what triggered them in those who

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.280
read its pages.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.040
It was found that those who read only the
first half of the book and stopped would be

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.220
completely fine.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:20.410
But those who read the book past the point
where the events began to shift away from

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:25.840
recorded history, otherwise known as the Point
of Divergence, would begin to experience the

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.520
adverse effects.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.010
Once a subject passed the Point of Divergence,
they would begin to accept all of the divergent

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.740
events described as absolute fact.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:38.720
If someone attempted to speak with them about
the differences between the divergent events

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:44.080
and real recorded history, the subject would
become upset and agitated.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.180
Even subjects who lived near the location
of events described in the book formed new,

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:53.190
vivid memories revolving around personal experiences
related to the event.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.190
Even if the content of the memories could
be debunked, no matter what they would insist

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.230
that what they had read in the book was the
truth.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.950
As they progressed deeper into the book, physical
symptoms would then begin to manifest.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:09.840
Usually, these began to appear around ten
years after the Point of Divergence and would

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.130
worsen as the mental symptoms became more
severe.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:17.380
One subject’s widow noticed a scar on his
body after his death, which had appeared during

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:19.430
the course of his exposure to the book.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:23.940
She was surprised to see it, and said that
she had not noticed it before.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.170
The Foundation became increasingly concerned
with learning how the book worked.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.250
What was it that made it affect people this
way?

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:35.820
Its influence was both physical and mental,
suggesting a possible combination of both

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.970
memetic and chemical effects.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:42.700
Dr. Grayson and the Foundation’s Chemical
Forensics team set about studying the chemical

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:48.940
properties of SCP-592, in order to determine
if its pages contained any substances that

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:53.190
could explain its disastrous effects on the
human mind and body.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:57.780
Small squares of paper were cut from several
pages of the book, cut so small that no more

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.900
than one word was contained on each square.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.820
The squares were then analyzed and screened
for any anomalies.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:09.350
When the results came back, Dr. Grayson and
his team were deeply disappointed.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:14.200
The book’s pages are made of standard cellulose
and wood, printed with completely ordinary

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.950
black and yellow inks.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:21.000
There are some unusual chemicals present in
the cyan and magenta inks used - suggesting

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.970
it was perhaps made in a location or plane
where chemical quantities differ - but none

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:30.880
of them are unknown to science, nor could
they be responsible for any of the damage

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.860
the book has done to the people that read
it.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:38.330
This meant that the book’s effects cannot
be explained away by a new chemical compound

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:43.290
or sophisticated bioweapon, something that
the Chemical Forensics department could study

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.740
and develop an antidote for.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:51.790
No, SCP-592 is much more mysterious and much
more powerful than that.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:58.780
SCP-592 is contained in research cell 1611-E
in a steel box in the middle of a frosted

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:00.130
glass cubicle.

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:05.240
In the same cubicle is a table, two computers,
a scanner, an internal network connection

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:10.310
port, and two pairs of goggles which must
be immediately put on by anyone inside the

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:11.410
cubicle.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:16.770
These goggles function to distort the text
and images of 592, rendering it impossible

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:19.620
for anyone wearing them to read while wearing
them.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.150
The first of the two computers is an analysis
machine, while the second one functions as

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.540
a firewall.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:29.880
Both computers have been outfitted with custom
software and hardware in accordance with the

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:35.339
Testing Protocol, and the network port cannot
be used by any device other than the firewall.

00:08:35.339 --> 00:08:39.760
The computers and the scanner are kept off
when they are not being used in an experiment

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:44.450
and must be immediately turned off following
the completion of any experimentation.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:50.330
The front and back covers of SCP-592 must
be covered in thick black tape at all times.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:52.600
So what is the testing protocol?

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:56.990
Unscrambled human eyes are no longer permitted
to look at the contents of the deadly book,

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:00.190
so the Foundation had to come up with an alternative.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:05.140
Since computers aren’t capable of experiencing
psychological distress - well, most of them

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:10.860
aren’t, SCP-079 might beg to differ of course
- the research team decided to find a way

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.320
to analyze the book using a computer system.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:19.100
For all testing, the book is scanned one page
at a time, and then sent into the analysis

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.100
machine.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.740
The machine has been modified so that it does
not store the original scanned version of

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:29.360
the image, and instead converts it promptly
into an analyzed version of the original content.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:33.510
The image is then promptly erased from the
system’s RAM as soon as possible.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:39.150
This process allows the research team to study
the contents of SCP-592, without exposing

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:43.490
themselves or any other human subjects to
the adverse effects of the book.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:47.830
Because those under the influence of the book’s
effects are unreliable witnesses, this is

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:53.330
considered the only way to ascertain an accurate,
neutral understanding of what is written in

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.230
these cursed pages.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:10:00.360
There are two different analysis protocols
in place: one for analysis of text, and one

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.500
for analysis of images.

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.740
Because understanding of the book’s specific
language could trigger adverse effects, and

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:11.270
drive the remaining members of the research
team to madness, the computer analysis of

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:15.820
the text must be as vague as possible while
still providing necessary context.

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:21.060
The language used is analytical in tone, describing
the subject matter discussed, the tone of

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:25.940
the original entry, and any incidents related
to the specific passage.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:31.940
For example, one piece of text analysis is
as follows: “The passage is describing human

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.940
conflict.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:43.660
The human conflict is of an ideological or
religious nature.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:44.950
The passage seems to be lamenting in tone.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.460
The passage contains the numbers 2000, 1977,
and 16…It is certain (98%) that the passage

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:53.520
contains a reference to both SCP [REDACTED]
and SCP [REDACTED].”

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.060
Not especially descriptive, but that’s the
point.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.150
Anything more detailed, and the research team
- not to mention everyone watching this video

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:04.700
at home - might be susceptible to the effects
of SCP-592.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:10.339
For a clearer picture of how unsettling the
book’s contents can get, we have to turn

00:11:10.339 --> 00:11:13.430
to, well, the pictures.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:17.920
SCP-592 contains approximately two hundred
illustrations.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:21.990
When a scanned page inputted into the computer
includes an image, it is put through several

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:26.970
convolutions and transforms in order to analyze
and summarize its contents in a manner safe

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.650
for human consumption.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:31.170
The original image’s record is promptly
destroyed.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:36.480
It is during this process of image analysis
that things get even eerier than they already

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.480
were.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:42.290
The images in the book are not the sort of
thing you’d see in an ordinary history book.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:46.270
The general subject matter of the pictures
is what you might expect: people at various

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:51.120
points throughout the 20th century, photographed
at historically significant events or just

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.709
living their regular lives during a significant
time period.

00:11:54.709 --> 00:11:56.970
But something about them…is wrong.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:12:01.290
While one Researcher was looking through the
computer analysis of the book, he came across

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:04.380
an image analysis that made his blood run
cold.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:09.050
The page read, in simple text:
“Date: 1st April 1963.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:12.910
Location: Unknown bedroom with Western furnishings.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.480
Type: Full color photograph.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:20.200
Subject: The image contains two adult persons
standing, one human child sitting on a chair

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:23.589
or stool, and SCP-[Redacted].

00:12:23.589 --> 00:12:31.060
With 100% certainty the persons in the image
should have facial features.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:36.160
With 100% certainty the persons in the image
do not have facial features.”

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:42.860
Now go check out “SCP-1025 - Encyclopedia
of Common Diseases” and “SCP-1230 - A

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:46.630
Hero Is Born” for more spellbinding book-based
anomalies!

